      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KEIKOKU (3) has the strongest current form, winning a Quality at this track two starts back before finishing second to One Destiny at Moruya, beaten just over a length after settling rearward and covering ground. He is third-up and back to the scene of the fresh win. Can round them up from the back. Stablemate IOWNA BENZ (6) resumes after a plain final run at Canberra Acton, but her broader record is strong, including a BM82 third at Dubbo and a previous win from one start at this track. Can sit up front from the outset under Fitzgerald and will take some catching. TEYLU (2) was beaten as favourite first-up at Moruya, though his record around 1000m and on good tracks keeps him in the mix if sharper second-up. ACTION KING (1) returns from a five-week let-up after finishing third behind KEIKOKU in Quality grade at this venue and he meets that runner better at the weights today. VELLA FOX (5) can fire a shot first-up.",
